<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">American South</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as antebellum American South</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The American South refers to the southern states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, where plantation agriculture relied on enslaved African labour before the Civil War. The antebellum South is often used as a point of comparison in discussions of large-scale <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> refer to it when describing the scale of plantation slavery in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>'s economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-south.jpg" alt="American South" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andrew_Jackson_monument,_New_Orleans,_USA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
